# Confidentiality gate - ONE list of exceptions for two layers: layer 2
# (structural-clause-modal) and layer 3, the identity layer (identity-*).
#
# Three distinguishable line forms:
# 1. A path pattern WITHOUT a prefix - a layer 2 exception, exactly as before.
# 2. `identity-value:<value>` - a layer 3 address declaration, in force across
#    the whole tree regardless of the file (an address is an INVENTORY, not an
#    allowlist: it has to occur at least once in the tree, otherwise the
#    completeness gate turns red).
# 3. `identity-path:<rule or all>:<pattern>` - a path exception narrowed to ONE
#    layer 3 rule, or - with the word `all` - to every rule at once. An
#    exception for one rule does NOT lift the others from the same path.
# A line starting with `identity-` that matches neither of the two prefixes
# above (or an `identity-path:` with a rule name outside the closed set) is a
# LOADING ERROR - not a silent path pattern.
#
# Layer 0 (the path layer, standards/.local) and layer 1 (the corpus layer)
# have NO exceptions here and never will - writing one here would contradict
# the purpose of those layers.
#
# The two test files below inherently contain invented sentences of normative
# shape as test data (never a real quote of a standard - see Pitfall 6 in
# 01-RESEARCH.md), so they are the only justified entries.
tests/test_confidentiality_guard.py
tests/test_confidentiality_guard_integration.py
tests/test_review_blockers_01.py

