# This entry is of a DIFFERENT class than the four above: `analysis.json`
# contains no invented sentence of normative shape - it contains
# `dump_deterministic` output (one string with no line breaks, a separator
# without whitespace). Layer 2 splits a fragment on SENTENCE TERMINATORS (full
# stop, exclamation mark, question mark), and minified JSON has very few of
# them (only inside text values), so a single "fragment" between two such
# terminators stretches over thousands of characters where in prose it would
# be one sentence. Measured 2026-09-06: a fragment reaching from the field
# `rubric_version":"1.0"` (which matches the shape of a clause number) to a
# modal word in an entirely unrelated sentence of `zones.py`, hundreds of JSON
# fields further on - two unrelated fragments of text, joined by the absence
# of full stops between them in the serialized JSON, not a quote of a
# standard. The impact is bounded to THIS file: `dump_deterministic` is the
# same function for every `analysis.json` in the project, but no other such
# file is tracked by git (the output directories are gitignored) - this is the
# first and only committed artifact of that shape.
examples/4sics/analysis.json

# --- Exceptions to the proper name rule (identity-project-name), D-23 ------
#
# The entries below are the only exceptions to that rule in the whole
# repository. Each is narrowed to ONE rule: an address from the employer's
# network or a device name in any of these files still trips the remaining
# layer 3 rules.

# The exception list file itself: a file that declares an exception for this
# rule has to be allowed to name what it is lifting, in the comment that
# justifies it.
identity-path:identity-project-name:.confidentiality-allow

# The gate file itself: the `PROJECT_NAME_PATTERN` pattern carries both words
# of the name as a literal, because otherwise it would have nothing to match
# against. The alternative - assembling the literal from parts at run time in
# order to avoid tripping its own rule - is circumventing the gate without
# changing its behaviour, exactly the anti-pattern this phase forbids
# elsewhere (assumption Z-96).
identity-path:identity-project-name:scripts/confidentiality_guard.py

